{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1498111-confused-about-the-bonsam","id":1498111,"title":"Confused about the Bonsam","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-11-26T23:22:36-08:00","id":1498111,"title":"Confused about the Bonsam","content":"I read over V20DA and I'm trying to find what power or merit gives the Bonsam their &quot;Batform,&quot; seen in their depicted art. The only real ability in their Disciplines that allow them access to concrete transformations is Abobwe, but none of the dot-powers within the Discipline itself doesn't have anything that'd relate to transforming into a Batform.<br /> <br /> Abobwe 2 has &quot;Invoking the Predator&quot; that lets you take up some aspects of predatory creatures, but it only allows small bits and parts of what you can emulate. <br /> <br /> Abobwe 5, &quot;Predator's Transformation,&quot; allows you to fully take up the appearance and full-on aspects of any predatory animal's heart you consume, but it just makes you into the animal itself; not a hybrid seen in the art depiction for the Bonsam Clan.<br /> <br /> Abobwe 6, &quot;Incarnate Darkness,&quot; just lets you become a mass of black shadow, something similar to what the Lasombra can do, but nothing about a &quot;Batform&quot; at all. <br /> <br /> I gripe about this because their Clan Weakness is doubly confusing: &quot;Mortals who fail a Courage roll (diff 7) when seeing a Bonsam in his <b>true form</b> either flee in terror or gather up weapons to kill the monster.&quot;<br /> <br /> What true form are they talking about? Does the embrace into becoming a Bonsam making you look like something of vague bat-like humanoid? If so, where are the merits to display this? Or do the Bonsam literally look human (as a Vampire can be, that is), but just have people fear them when looking at them no matter what?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-27T08:47:49-08:00","id":1498127,"title":"","content":"The way i read it, the bat-form is how they look after the embrace. The &quot;true form&quot; effect is when they are seen without obfuscate. Given that they seem to be a Nosfreatu based bloodline...<br /> <br /> Not the best write up, but that's what i got from it...<br /> <br /> Not sure what you mean by &quot;where are the merits to display this? &quot; though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Prone to being a Classic Curmudgeon, goshdarned whippersnappers...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1037-jamiemalk","name":"jamiemalk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1037_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}